@* Each day is a real radio input, so choosing one posts under `day` with no JavaScript at all,
   and the browser supplies the arrow keys, Home and End within the group. For picking one date in
   a form, <DatePicker> around <input type="date"> is smaller still — this is for when the shape
   of the month is the information. *@
<Calendar Name="day" Month="@(new DateOnly(2026, 3, 1))"
          Selected="@(new DateOnly(2026, 3, 11))"
          Today="@(new DateOnly(2026, 3, 11))"
          Disabled="@(d => d.DayOfWeek is DayOfWeek.Saturday or DayOfWeek.Sunday)"
          Class="w-fit rounded-lg border p-3" />
